\f0\b Facilitator:
\f1\b0  Great. So, let\'92s begin simply\'97how are you, where do you live, what do you do, and where are you in your life right now?\

\f0\b Participant:
\f1\b0  I\'92m 33 and live in Connecticut, USA. I\'92m married and a new mother of a six-and-a-half-month-old baby. I work in cloud tech, and that\'92s pretty much the main context right now. I used to travel a lot\'97an ex-world traveler\'97but now I\'92m home, raising a child.\

\f0\b Facilitator:
\f1\b0  What are your main priorities at this stage of life?\

\f0\b Participant:
\f1\b0  My biggest priority is childcare. I can\'92t really access my old identities\'97traveling, blogging, photography. Those belonged to another chapter.\
Now it\'92s my baby, food, and sleep. Making sure we\'92re all fed and rested feels like the whole job some days. Health should be higher on the list\'97it\'92s not yet\'97but it has to be.\

\f0\b Facilitator:
\f1\b0  Do you feel like you\'92re in the right place right now, or do you wish things were different?\

\f0\b Participant:
\f1\b0  I feel I\'92m in the right place\'97this is where my partner and I worked hard to get to. We\'92ve had many surprises, but we don\'92t want to give up on the dream we built together.\
There\'92s also an immigration aspect\'97my husband\'92s green-card process and all that\'97so we manifested this life, but as you know, when you manifest something, it\'92s rarely exactly what you imagined.\
The last chapter we lived in Georgia was very rural and humble\'97a totally different rhythm from capitalist America with all its comfort. Part of me misses that simplicity and being close to nature. But for this chapter, with a baby, I\'92m in the right place. I need more support now.\

\f0\b Facilitator:
\f1\b0  Comfort and stability.\

\f0\b Participant:
\f1\b0  Exactly. Many women do the village-life-with-baby thing and I respect them deeply, but maybe it\'92s easier for those who grew up like that. I didn\'92t. I miss my culture sometimes, which is why we decided to move back to the States when I became pregnant.\
So yes, I\'92m in the right space for now\'97but I know it\'92s not forever. I\'92d like to return to that simpler lifestyle once my child is older, maybe when he\'92s big enough to explore nature.\
If I spent my time thinking I made a mistake, I\'92d just fall into depression\'97and it\'92s not even true, because who knows what\'92s a mistake? This is just a chapter. It\'92s not easy, but it\'92s right for this stage. Nothing\'92s permanent.\

\f0\b Facilitator:
