\f0\b Facilitator:
\f1\b0  What eventually helped you find someone who didn\'92t trigger that pattern so strongly?\

\f0\b Participant:
\f1\b0  Near the end of my \'93sad-girl anxious-attachment era,\'94 I joined a friend\'92s online course from Mexico. It mixed 
\f0\b shadow-work prompts
\f1\b0  and 
\f0\b celibacy practice
\f1\b0 . The shadow work made me look at triggers and re-program them; the celibacy part was radical\'97I vowed to stop engaging with men completely.\
I was heartbroken, exhausted from dating men who loved my free spirit but didn\'92t want real partnership. My heart\'92s too big for temporary romance. So I stopped sex, stopped makeup, stopped dressing for attention. I cut off the male gaze entirely\'97no flirting, no DMs, nothing.\
That year of celibacy was my reset. I told myself, \'93Maybe I\'92ll never have children. Maybe I\'92ll just travel and be a cool aunt.\'94 One night, during a breakdown, I finally prayed, 
\f2\i Take away my hope for love; I can\'92t bear it anymore.
\f1\i0 \
